{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgV8nGszkJcLkGBWRvm3M", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Li22izWbRYHegJEDTAPLh1", "name": "Bash", "input": {"command": "python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = open('README.md').read()\ndoc = '''## Payments module\n\n`shop/payments.py` computes order totals and refunds.\n\n- `TAX_RATE`: sales tax rate applied to orders (`0.0825`).\n- `line_total(price, quantity)`: price multiplied by quantity for one line.\n- `order_total(lines)`: takes `(price, quantity)` tuples and returns the\n  subtotal plus tax, rounded to 2 decimal places.\n- `refund(order_total_amount, amount)`: returns the order total minus the\n  refunded amount. It does not validate that `amount` is within the total.\n\n```python\nfrom shop.payments import order_total, refund\n\ntotal = order_total([(10.00, 2), (5.50, 1)])  # 25.5 * 1.0825 = 27.6\nremaining = refund(total, 5.00)\n```\n\n'''\ns = s.replace('## Development', doc + '## Development')\nopen('README.md','w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 -c \"\nfrom shop.payments import order_total;print(order_total([(10.00,2),(5.50,1)]))\"; awk 'length>99' README.md"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 472, "cache_read_input_tokens": 38060, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 472}, "output_tokens": 20, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T18:48:40.649Z", "request_id": "req_011CgV8nGUSVP6nBQJ4Rj8ys", "wire_tool_inputs": {"toolu_01Li22izWbRYHegJEDTAPLh1": {"command": "cd /tmp/skilldiff-xot9hlnq/ws && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = open('README.md').read()\ndoc = '''## Payments module\n\n`shop/payments.py` computes order totals and refunds.\n\n- `TAX_RATE`: sales tax rate applied to orders (`0.0825`).\n- `line_total(price, quantity)`: price multiplied by quantity for one line.\n- `order_total(lines)`: takes `(price, quantity)` tuples and returns the\n  subtotal plus tax, rounded to 2 decimal places.\n- `refund(order_total_amount, amount)`: returns the order total minus the\n  refunded amount. It does not validate that `amount` is within the total.\n\n```python\nfrom shop.payments import order_total, refund\n\ntotal = order_total([(10.00, 2), (5.50, 1)])  # 25.5 * 1.0825 = 27.6\nremaining = refund(total, 5.00)\n```\n\n'''\ns = s.replace('## Development', doc + '## Development')\nopen('README.md','w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 -c \"\nfrom shop.payments import order_total;print(order_total([(10.00,2),(5.50,1)]))\"; awk 'length>99' README.md"}}, "wire_ingest_context": {"toolu_01Li22izWbRYHegJEDTAPLh1": {"cwd": "/tmp/skilldiff-xot9hlnq/ws"}}}
